      "desc": "Primary enclosures.",
      "narrative": "Several of the metal ceiling beams in the off-exhibit nonhuman primate enclosures have flaking paint and rust. The areas\nof rust range in size from a few inches to feet in length.\nFailure to maintain primary enclosures can lead to loose paint, rust, or exposed surfaces which can allow for ingestion of\nforeign materials and make cleaning difficult.\nPrimary enclosures must be constructed of suitable materials and kept in good repair to ensure the health of the animals.\nCorrect by: 07/20/2026.\nThis inspection and exit interview were conducted with facility representatives.\nAdditional Inspectors:\nTonya Hadjis, Supervisory Animal Care Specialist n"
